      "side": 1,
      "message": "I don\u0027t understand why the GSC needs to waste time verifying this? These ranges are already signed and trusted, we should assume that they contain what they\u0027re meant to contain. (Also, the FMAP being covered is not actually a requirement of the design. The way RO verification is designed for coreboot, only the bootblock needs to be verified and then it contains the information needed to verify any other data loaded later itself, including the FMAP.)",
      "revId": "e272a15aab408f1d370ed0383f3db203106dabe0",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
