        "id": 1353551
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-09-28T08:38:33Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e verify_ranges() first reads the ranges values from AP flash, note that this function is shared by the old and new AP RO verification flows.\n\nThe only caller of verify_ranges() is ap_ro_check_version2(). How is it shared by the old flow?\n\n\u003e The ranges values are needed for GVD verification. I agree that we could read the ranges values first, then verify GVD and then verify the ranges, but this would cause some code expansion for no particularly good reason.\n\nSince the ranges array is considered part of the GVD structure, I think we can read it directly inside read_gscvd(). Then\n\n- gvd_cache_check()\n- read_signature_header(), read_keyblock()\n- verify_gvd_signature() (with shared_mem_release(sig_body) inside)\n- unpack_pubk(), verify_keyblock() and shared_mem_release(rootkc.rootk)\n- Read ranges from SPI flash, and validate_ranges_sha()\n\nThis way we won\u0027t use more memory compared to current PS, and we only need to change the current code by a little bit. What do you think?",
      "parentUuid": "7f576ae8_18168439",
      "revId": "e272a15aab408f1d370ed0383f3db203106dabe0",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
